{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1203781-backing-up-yourself","id":1203781,"title":"Backing up yourself.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-06T03:58:01-07:00","id":1203781,"title":"Backing up yourself.","content":"Hey All.<br /> <br /> I watched Altered Carbon the other day and the idea of performing backups on oneself made me wonder.<br /> <br /> So the whole premise for those that haven't watched the show is that the mind/soul of a person is basically completely divorced from your body as you can via technology change bodies (or sleeves as they are called in the show) like you change clothes (if you have the cash). You have your mind/soul in what's called a stack, an alien device that gets surgically implanted at the age of 1. As long as your stack is ok you can insert that into another body upon your death. Normally you can die for real if your stack is destroyed but some people with enough money have found a way to backup their stacks into the Cloud. These people are rich enough to afford clones of themselves as well so they are basically immortal.<br /> <br /> So my question is, what would it take to back yourself up in terms of Spheres (including the Avatar) and what would this look like for the various Conventions and Traditions?<br /> <br /> Would Mind 5/Spirit 5 be enough to move to another body or do you need to add Life as well? Life 5 would obviously be needed for cloning though.<br /> <br /> My thoughts for the Conventions would be similar to the show in that there is an implanted device that can be backed up to a Cloud, with Progenitor grown clones serving as sleeves.<br /> <br /> Hermetics would perhaps use external Phylacteries similar to old school liches. I doubt Verbena, Euthantos, Akashics and Dreamspeakers would like this at all for various reasons but i'm curious anyway.<br /> <br /> Let me know your thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T07:20:29-07:00","id":1203820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1203781-backing-up-yourself#post1203781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey All.<br /> <br /> I watched Altered Carbon the other day and the idea of performing backups on oneself made me wonder.<br /> <br /> So the whole premise for those that haven't watched the show is that the mind/soul of a person is basically completely divorced from your body as you can via technology change bodies (or sleeves as they are called in the show) like you change clothes (if you have the cash). You have your mind/soul in what's called a stack, an alien device that gets surgically implanted at the age of 1. As long as your stack is ok you can insert that into another body upon your death. Normally you can die for real if your stack is destroyed but some people with enough money have found a way to backup their stacks into the Cloud. These people are rich enough to afford clones of themselves as well so they are basically immortal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My thoughts for the Conventions would be similar to the show in that there is an implanted device that can be backed up to a Cloud, with Progenitor grown clones serving as sleeves.<br /> <br /> Hermetics would perhaps use external Phylacteries similar to old school liches. I doubt Verbena, Euthantos, Akashics and Dreamspeakers would like this at all for various reasons but i'm curious anyway.<br /> <br /> Let me know your thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, this kind of magick isn't uncommon among Masters. Progenitors in particular are famous for having backup clones of themselves, and for providing such service to other Conventions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So my question is, what would it take to back yourself up in terms of Spheres (including the Avatar) and what would this look like for the various Conventions and Traditions?<br /> Would Mind 5/Spirit 5 be enough to move to another body or do you need to add Life as well? Life 5 would obviously be needed for cloning though. </div> </div> </div>I think you got it right.<br /> <br /> If you want to keep your soul in a &quot;safe&quot; place (like, say, a Phylactery), Spirit 5 it's the way to go, probably with Prime 4 to make the object into a magical soul vessel of sorts (which it's quite a supernatural property if you ask me).<br /> <br /> However, If you want to move both Mind and Soul, some would argue that Mind 5 replaces Spirit in that Rote, because you don't need Spirit to use magick trough an Astral Body - the soul seems to travel with the mind, and thus Spirit wouldn't be necessary. Even when the Silver Cord that joins Mind and Body it's cutt, the mage can still use magick while he's in an astral body. But that's at ST discretion, maybe Spirit it's still needed to create a vessel that can hold a soul indefinitely. Maybe it isn't needed but it helps to offset the consequences...<br /> <br /> Now, talking about consequences, to connect the mind &amp; soul to an unliving body may have unforeseen consequences: Using the Lich rote a mage assumes an undead form that can still sustain True Magick, but can't increase Arete as a consequence of the inherent Statism of such form - I would argue that a purely material object would be as much if not more statical. Thus, to turn your body for something less mortal may have undesirable consequences, like becoming unable to increase Arete or worse, at ST discretion.<br /> <br /> Now, Mind 5 allows you to get an Astral Body and to posses people - this allows to act at distance. To create the body Life 5 it's a must.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hermetics would perhaps use external Phylacteries similar to old school liches. </div> </div> </div>Hermetics would do that. However, to become an undead abomination it's extremely forbidden (because the Tremere) and thus they would probably preffert to posses a Golem or some thing like that (assuming that joining your soul to matter isn't even more blasphemous and damaging, of course)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I doubt Verbena, Euthantos, Akashics and Dreamspeakers would like this at all for various reasons but i'm curious anyway. </div> </div> </div>Euthanatos were the first to invent the Lich rote, but also the first to ban it (and created the Nagaraja while they were at it).<br /> <br /> Akashicks have a sort of cloud backup already in the form of the akashic record - they just take their time to change between bodies. I'm not sure they would be opposed to this. On one hand they revere life and movement, but on the other they revere the ideal of transcending material limitations - one may say that creating your own bodies it's just that.<br /> <br /> Verbena revere life, they would NEVER join an unliving object.<br /> <br /> However, I could see a Verbena (an Akashic or Euthanatos too) being more confortable transforming into a tree. The witch could fuse her soul with a tree or even a full grove, and then creating bodies to inhabit out of it's fruits or roots.<br /> <br /> Doing so would require, <i>at least,</i> Prime 5 and Mind 5. Life 5 to create the bodies. Correspondence 5 if you want to spread your consciousness trough a whole grove.<br /> <br /> Again, being a tree may have *consequences*, at St discretion, albeit I would argue a tree it's less statical than a Lich (the latter being a half-corpse preserved through magick).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T09:51:38-07:00","id":1203871,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your reply Aleph. But just to clarify, i'm not talking about some undead form, i'm talking about moving from one living body to another. So if a mage dies his mind and soul and avatar would be able to move to a new body (most probably grown with Life 5) or if you want to be rally nasty move into and take over the body of another being, pushing their mind out of the body and stealing it. Or taking over a body of someone who is braindead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T10:38:20-07:00","id":1203888,"title":"","content":"Mage20 actually describes similar effects in the Wonders section. &quot;The Rebooter Self-Retrieval Bio-Printer&quot; pretty much makes a save-state of your current form and reprints you as you were when you used to be then, whenever you die. This one actually recreates you as you were on a very specific point of time. You will lose everything you gained afterwards (memories, experience, stats, etc).<br /> <br /> To &quot;simply&quot; move your body, I'd rule Spirit 5/Life 5 to take permanent possession of a body. Every lesser effect would be non-permanent and subjects your mage to pattern bleeding or possibly Permadox instead. Could be bought up with experience, eventually. But that's just how I would deal with this, from a storyteller perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T01:39:50-07:00","id":1204144,"title":"","content":"An option with possibly lower sphere levels:<br /> Telepresence<br /> (Correspondence 2+, Forces 2+, Mind 1+, optional Spirit 2+ and Prime 2)<br /> Shifting your perception(all senses) to a illusion(your body remains where it is, but your image is elsewhere) of yourself. Forces/Correspondence ports the needed telekinetic energy over. Mind provides multitasking.<br /> <br /> It may seem like you can switch bodies, survive deathtraps and the like. Best used from your Sanctum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}